# #5839 (#5833's lazy key-moving close in H): the shard root raises the routing generation
# durably, then defers L's close head, and L's arm resolves it.
MODULE: DeferredHeadAtRaisedGenerationDeferredHeadBeforeRaise
TARGET: DeferredHeadAtRaisedGeneration
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the deferred head is written before the raise is durable, naming the generation the raise will take, so a crash between the steps leaves L to re-claim a generation the shard root never raised and will later admit under
PERTURBS: CloseDefer
BOUNDS: WithPreArm = TRUE, WithDeferredClose = TRUE

--- FIND
CloseDefer ==
    /\ dfStage = "raised"
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ pend' = TRUE
    /\ pendGen' = fEpoch

--- REPLACE
CloseDefer ==
\* MUTATION: the deferred head first, naming the generation the raise will take.
    /\ WithDeferredClose
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ dfStage = "none"
    /\ ~pend
    /\ fEpoch < MaxEpoch
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ pend' = TRUE
    /\ pendGen' = fEpoch + 1

--- END
